# NFILT (enter a filter: wavelength / flux pairs, 0 ends), SFILT (write it as <name>.filt), RFILT (read it back),
# MULTISPEC (the multi-color stack) on a COPY of the manual's Cassegrain in $TMP (cmdref: Source & Wavelength).
# Measured 2026-10-17 (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (o)): NFILT reports 2 wavelengths and 1 star type, SFILT writes the
# file, RFILT reads it back with 0 STAR TYPES, and MULTISPEC then refuses every star type ("Invalid star type") --
# the written and read filter formats disagree on the star-type count, so MULTISPEC cannot be fed from NFILT.
# Before any filter is loaded MULTISPEC says "Load filter data first."  This journal pins what is measured.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
cd $TMP
old $DECK
none
multispec
nfilt
myfilt
6.0e-7
1.0
6.5e-7
0.5
0
sfilt
myfilt
rfilt
myfilt
multispec
5
1
! ls $TMP
# EXPECT: Load filter data first\.
# EXPECT: Filter includes information for\s+2 wavelengths and\s+1 star types\.
# EXPECT: Filter file created\.
# EXPECT: MACOS> rfilt\s+Enter filter file name: myfilt\s+Filter includes information for\s+2 wavelengths and\s+0 star types\.
# EXPECT: Enter StarType \(1-0\): \[1\]: 1\s+Invalid star type\.
# EXPECT: myfilt\.filt
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
